<title>UK: Smith &amp; Nephew shares up on bid speculation.</title>
<headline>Smith &amp; Nephew shares up on bid speculation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Smith &amp; Nephew Plc jumped on Friday after the Daily Mail newspaper said speculators were piling into the stock on talk that U.S. drugs group Eli Lilley was planning a bid for the UK healthcare firm.</p>
<p>Smith &amp; Nephew shares climbed as high as 196p in early trade. By 0907 GMT they were up 4-1/4p at 192-1/4.  </p>
<p>The Mail said several investors had bought stock shortly before the close on Thursday on the back of speculation that Eli Lilley would launch a bid of 260p per share.</p>
<p>&quot;We saw a bit of speculative buying yesterday and the newspaper article has encouraged even more today,&quot; one market-maker said. &quot;It's very vague talk but you don't want to be short.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
